  "notes": [
    "The two llama.cpp tiers disagree on the prefill verdict and the artifact keeps both rather than promoting one. At the llama-bench tier llama.cpp HIP leads prefill at every shape; at the explicit-token-array binding tier hipEngine leads at 512/1K and trails at 4K.",
    "llama-bench generates its own prompts and cannot accept the repeated-token prompt the hipEngine sweep uses, so the llama-bench tier is a split-timing/profile comparator and not a token-exact one.",
    "llama-bench decode is decode-at-offset (-p 0 -n 128 -d <prompt>), which is not the same timing scope as a resident-session AR decode after a real prefill.",
    "hipEngine tracked_peak_gib covers hipEngine allocator ownership only; llama GTT delta is a whole-process external sample. The two columns are different scopes and are not a memory-advantage claim.",
    "Correctness gates on the hipEngine side are unchanged from the refresh this supersedes: stable finite final token 9707 at every shape, tracked teardown to zero, CV far under the 5% gate.",
    "A pre-existing defect was hit while running the comparator: hipengine/benchmark/provenance.py resolves device_name via ctypes.CDLL('libamdhip64.so'), which is not on the default loader path on a TheRock-only host, so the artifact write failed after all six llama-bench cells had completed. The comparator was rerun inside the hermetic TheRock environment. scripts/run_gfx1151_readme_refresh.sh runs its llamacpp phase without that environment."
  ]
